          "text_excerpt": "{\n  \"studies\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 23696,\n      \"is_similar\": false,\n      \"description\": \"<p>This study is evaluating experimental antiviral treatments for cats diagnosed with <strong>feline infectious peritonitis (FIP)</strong>, including both the <strong>effusive (“wet”)</strong> and <strong>non-effusive (“dry”)</strong> forms of the disease.</p><p>FIP is a serious viral disease caused by feline coronavirus (FCoV). Researchers are studying different treatment options to better understand their safety and effectiveness in cats with FIP.</p><p>Cats enrolled in the study may receive different experimental antiviral treatments depending on the needs of the patient and study protocol. Cats will be closely monitored throughout the study period to evaluate response to treatment and overall health.</p>\",\n      \"absolute_url\": \"https://clinicaltrials.csuveterinaryhealth.org/s/new-treatments-for-fip-feline-infectious-peritonitis-827121/?ref=gallery\",\n      \"tagline\": \"New Hope for FIP\",\n      \"name\": \"New Treatments for FIP (Feline Infectious Peritonitis)\",\n      \"visible_sc_items\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": 970,\n          \"tag_path\": \"primary-field_blood/tissue/urine-collection\",\n          \"label\": \"Blood/Tissue/Urine Collection\",\n          \"parent_label\": \"Topics\",\n          \"show_as_attribute_on_card\": false,\n          \"icon\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": 944,\n          \"tag_path\": \"animals_Cats\",\n          \"label\": \"Cats\",\n          \"parent_label\": \"Animals\",\n          \"show_as_attribute_on_card\": false,\n          \"icon\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": 966,\n          \"tag_path\": \"primary-field_infections\",\n          \"label\": \"Infections\",\n          \"parent_label\": \"Topics\",\n          \"show_as_attribute_on_card\": false,\n          \"icon\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": 979,\n          \"tag_path