          "text_excerpt": "ESVONC CONGRESS | Clinical Trials - Ongoing EU Clinical Trials Menu Home Discover our society Objectives Board Become a ESVONC member History Other Societies National Veterinary Oncology Societies Veterinary Oncology Societies in the world Congress Venue City Scotland Accessibility Congress Venue Hotels Abstract Submission Guidelines on how to write a scientific abstract Guidelines after acceptance on how to present an oral communication or poster Instructions for abstract submission Registration Social Program Sponsors and Exhibitors Sponsorship information Platinum Sponsors Bronze Sponsors Speakers Awards Congress Calendar Picture Gallery Nurses ESVONC Nurses Membership Education Portal How to get involved Clinical Research Ongoing Clinical trials Clinical Research Fund News Job offers Education Courses Clinical Trials Internship Framework Contact Members Log-In Ongoing EU Clinical Trials ESVONC attaches great importance to innovation and evidence-based medicine in the field of veterinary oncology. Therefore, we are happy to share with you with a monthly overview of ongoing canine and feline oncology trials in Europe. We are convinced that knowledge of these trials will enhance collaboration between researchers and clinicians, thus increasing recruitment for clinical trials and treatment options for dogs and cats. Please find below a non-exhaustive listing of ongoing trials as gathered in the Oncowaf database. For more details about these trials, please visit https://oncowaf.be/en/ClinicalTrials . If you have an ongoing clinical trial and would like to add it to the Oncowaf clinical trial database and this mailing, please contact contact@oncowaf.com . This list is an intiative of dr. Laetitia Cicchelero (DVM, PhD, Cross-health coordinator @ Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, Ghent University). Laetitia is initiator and inspirer of ONCOWAF. ESVONC wishes to thank Laetitia for her efforts to create this useful overview. This list is updated o