          "text_excerpt": "Clinical trials - School of Veterinary Science - University of Queensland Skip to menu Skip to content Skip to footer Menu Study Research Partners and community About Search School of Veterinary Science Home About About Welcome\" > Welcome Our people\" > Our people Accreditation\" > Accreditation History\" > History News\" > News Events\" > Events Strategic plan\" > Strategic plan Equity, diversity and inclusion\" > Equity, diversity and inclusion Staff intranet\" > Staff intranet Study Study Undergraduate\" > Undergraduate Honours\" > Honours Higher Degree by Research (HDR)\" > Higher Degree by Research (HDR) Research Research Research themes\" > Research themes Collaborations and partnerships\" > Collaborations and partnerships Facilities\" > Facilities Services and hospitals Services and hospitals UQ VETS Equine Specialist Hospital\" > UQ VETS Equine Specialist Hospital UQ VETS Production Animal Service\" > UQ VETS Production Animal Service UQ VETS Small Animal Hospital\" > UQ VETS Small Animal Hospital Veterinary Laboratory Services\" > Veterinary Laboratory Services Pets for Life Adoption Program\" > Pets for Life Adoption Program Community Student support Student support Scholarships and prizes\" > Scholarships and prizes Student engagement\" > Student engagement Student Clinical Skills Hub\" > Student Clinical Skills Hub International students\" > International students North American Veterinary Licensing Examination (NAVLE)\" > North American Veterinary Licensing Examination (NAVLE) Contact Study Research Partners and community About UQ home News Events Give Contact Search term UQ home News Events Give Contact School of Veterinary Science Menu Home About Show About sub-navigation Welcome Our people Accreditation History News Events Strategic plan Equity, diversity and inclusion Staff intranet Study Show Study sub-navigation Undergraduate Honours Higher Degree by Research (HDR) Research Show Research sub-navigation Research themes Collaborations and partnerships Facilities Services and hospitals Show Services and hospitals sub-navigation UQ VETS Equine Specialist Hospital UQ VETS Production Animal Service UQ VETS Small Animal Hospital Veterinary Laboratory Services Pets for Life Adoption Program Community Student support Show Student support sub-navigation Scholarships and prizes Student engagement Student Clinical Skills Hub International students North American Veterinary Licensing Examination (NAVLE) Contact Clinical trials Home Community The School of Veterinary Science has several clinical trials and research studies seeking volunteers and input from the public. Each trial or research study has varying requirements in regards to the assistance the investigators are requiring. We invite you to take a look at the current trials listed below to see if you can contribute. Please note that all clinical trials and research have animal ethics and/or human ethics approvals, participation is voluntary and any participants can be removed from a trial at any time. Dog bone cancer vaccine trial We are looking for pet dogs diagnosed with cancer to test an experimental vaccine. The clinical research trial is for dogs recently diagnosed with canine appendicular osteosarcoma, a common bone tumour that affects 10,000 dogs a year globally. In this trial, our researchers will assess two vaccine formulations. To be eligible, dogs need to have been diagnosed with appendicular osteosarcoma of long bones of the limbs with no evidence of metastasis, or cancer spread, based on a physical exam and radiographs. Dogs can be any breed but must be proceeding to surgery to treat their cancer. Read more about these trials . Applications for the trial can be made via this webform , or questions can be directed to Dr José Granados Soler . Cattle with lantana camara toxicity We are looking for cattle that are naturally intoxicated with lantana camara. Lantana is a common toxic plant in Queensland. We are searching for prognostic indicators of intoxicated cattle to better id",
