          "text_sha256": "e1400161917f957234ed4c41eeaf2f3470c80e753ede97c12910051701774766",
          "text_length": 3558,
          "text_excerpt": "Register Interest in Our Dog Cancer Trial | Gamgee GAMGEE Our mission Our story In the media Partnership Register interest Our mission Our story In the media Partnership Register interest Trial now recruiting · Australia Register your interest in our dog cancer trial We are recruiting dogs with mast cell cancer in Australia for an investigational trial of personalised mRNA cancer vaccines. Register your interest and share a few details about your dog. Our team will contact you about further screening. Register your interest → See how it works → Why we are running this trial From Rosie’s story to a future for more dogs. Rosie The first dog treated with a personalised neoantigen vaccine. It began with Rosie. Her experience with a personalised neoantigen vaccine encouraged Paul to explore how this approach could one day be made available to every dog with cancer. Before an approach like this can become broadly available, we must study it carefully and support it by evidence for review by the relevant veterinary regulators. This clinical trial is an important step in that process, helping us learn from participating dogs and understand the vaccine more fully. Read Rosie’s personalised mRNA cancer-vaccine story → Who can register If your dog has cancer and is currently in Australia, you’re welcome to register your interest. Our team will check whether your dog may be eligible for this trial. Register your interest → About the trial What this trial is looking at The trial will investigate a personalised mRNA vaccine approach for dogs with mast cell cancer. Tell us about your dog and our team will help determine whether they may be eligible for screening. Who can register Dogs diagnosed with mast cell cancer who are based in, or able to travel within, Australia. Every case is reviewed individually The trial approach A therapeutic mRNA vaccine designed from each dog’s own tumour and blood samples, intended to work alongside—not replace—existing care. Personalised to each dog What screening involves We help coordinate records, screening, sample logistics and updates, working with the trial team and your treating veterinarian. A named team stays in touch Trial registration and screening How to register your interest. You don’t need to have every record ready before registering your interest. Start with what you know and we’ll help with the rest. 01 Register your interest Complete a short form with basic details about your dog, their mast cell cancer diagnosis and where you live. 02 We get in touch A Gamgee coordinator will contact you, answer practical questions and—with your permission—help gather relevant records from your vet. 03 The trial team confirms eligibility The authorised study team and treating veterinarian assess potential eligibility. If your dog may proceed, you’ll receive the approved trial information and consent discussion before deciding. These are indicative timings from a single case. Sequencing turnaround and manufacturing schedules may vary. We will give you a case-specific estimate before proceeding. Ready to tell us about your dog? Registering your interest does not guarantee eligibility or enrolment. Please continue your dog's existing veterinary care while your information is reviewed. Register your interest → Gamgee updates Stay informed Get occasional updates on our research, clinical trials and progress in personalised cancer care for dogs. Your email address Join mailing list → One quick security check: × ✓ You’re on the list. Thank you for joining. We’ll keep you updated.",
