          "text_excerpt": "Veterinary Clinical Research & Trials | MediPaws Call 1800 678 387 233 Catherine St, Leichhardt About Close About Open About About MediPaws Our Story Meet Our Team Our Events Media Hub Our Facilities Cat Friendly Care Join Our Newsletter Careers With Us Where to Find Us Services Close Services Open Services Departments 24/7 Emergency Care Anaesthesia Surgery Internal Medicine Diagnostic Imaging Dermatology Oncology Ophthalmology Rehabilitation Medical Centres Main Procedures Departments 24/7 Emergency Care Anaesthesia Surgery Internal Medicine Diagnostic Imaging Oncology Partner Services Dermatology Ophthalmology Rehabilitation Medical Centres Nuclear Medicine Feline Medicine Kidney & Urinary Medicine Main Procedures TPLO Surgery THR Surgery Hydrotherapy Feline Radioiodine Bone Scan Clinic Clinical Research All Services Departments 24/7 Emergency Care Anaesthesia Surgery Internal Medicine Diagnostic Imaging Dermatology Oncology Ophthalmology Rehabilitation Other Services Nuclear Medicine Feline Medicine Kidney & Urinary Medicine TPLO Surgery THR Surgery Hydrotherapy Feline Radioiodine Bone Scan Clinic Meet Our Team Pet Owners Close Pet Owners Open Pet Owners For Pet Owners Your Visit At MediPaws Register Your Pet Fees & Payment Options Blood Donor Program Pet Advice Hub Stray Animals Where To Find Us Register Your Pet Vets & Nurses Close Vets & Nurses Open Vets & Nurses For Veterinary Professionals Refer A Patient Our Services Fixed Price Packages Peace of Mind Package Gap-Free Services Client Resources Education Events Ask a Specialist Publications The Fast Fetch Join Our Team Refer a Patient Contact 24/7 Emergency Clinical Research Home > Clinical Research Clinical Research at MediPaws Our commitment to advancing the field of veterinary medicine Advancing veterinary care is about delivering the best care today while learning how to improve care for future patients. Much like in human medicine, clinical research plays an important role in helping veterinarians refine treatments, reduce risk, and achieve better patient outcomes. Many of the treatments and approaches used at MediPaws and other veterinary hospitals have been shaped by ongoing research. Through these evidence-based findings, we are able to continually improve the safety and effectiveness of care for our beloved pets. Why participate in clinical research Many pet owners participate in clinical research knowing that their pet’s involvement may help improve care for other pets in the future. By participating in our no-harm studies, your pet can contribute to better treatments, reduced procedure risk, and improved quality of life for pets in the future around the world. Each study will provide specific information about any potential benefits for your pet. Depending on the research, this may include additional insight into recovery, monitoring, or complementary diagnostic testing. Why we're involved in clinical research​ At MediPaws, clinical research is a natural extension of our commitment to provide the highest standard of care possible. Every day, our teams manage complex emergency and referral cases across multiple specialties, giving us valuable insight into how treatments perform in real-world settings and what works best. Clinical research allows our specialists to keep asking important questions, including: How can we improve tests and treatments already in use? Can we reduce risks around anaesthesia, hospitalisation and recovery? What can we do to improve long-term outcomes and quality of life for patients? What “no-harm” clinical research means at MediPaws Our specialists take a no-harm approach to all clinical research, meaning every study is designed with patient welfare as the top priority. Research is carefully structured so it never compromises care, and often involves non-invasive data collection alongside routine treatment or comparing standard approaches already in use. Participation in any research at MediPaws is always: