          "text_excerpt": "Profile --> Regina Hayburn, DVM, DACVIM (oncology) Texas A&M College of Veterinary Medicine , Oncology Studies Evaluating whole abdomen radiation therapy as a treatment for feline small cell gastrointestinal lymphoma Help us determine if whole abdomen radiation therapy helps cats with small cell gastrointestinal lymphoma Evaluating whole abdomen radiation therapy as a treatment for feline small cell gastrointestinal lymphoma Help us determine if whole abdomen radiation therapy helps cats with small cell gastrointestinal lymphoma This study will evaluate how well-tolerated whole abdomen radiation is for cats diagnosed with small cell lymphoma.&nbsp;The goal of this study is to establish a safe and practical radiation protocol and to monitor treatment response in cats with gastrointestinal small cell lymphoma (i.e., cancer involving the stomach or intestines). Active - Recruiting oncology All, age any This study will evaluate how well-tolerated whole abdomen radiation is for cats diagnosed with small cell lymphoma.&nbsp;The goal of this study is to establish a safe and practical radiation protocol and to monitor treatment response in cats with gastrointestinal small cell lymphoma (i.e., cancer involving the stomach or intestines). Cancer Investigator Regina Hayburn, DVM, DACVIM (oncology) Learn More Cancer Privacy Policy Terms of Use 2026 Studypages by Yuzu Labs PBC",
