          "text_excerpt": "Pet Trial Finder — Clinical trial matching for dogs & cats Processing... Pet Trial Finder How it works Why trials? Cancer types Resources Registry Support Find trials — $7 Find trials — $7 Your vet knows cancer. They may not know about all 100 + active trials. We search every university research program in the country, find the trials your pet qualifies for, and handle the application on your behalf. Check Your Pet's Eligibility Now We only feature active trials from accredited universities nationwide. 100 + Active clinical trials tracked 25 Accredited university partners 34 Cancer types covered Cancers We Cover Active oncology clinical trials across 34 cancer types. Hover any segment to explore, or see the top conditions in the panel. 100 TOTAL TRIALS Active Enrollment — Top Conditions Osteosarcoma 27 trial s 15.7 % of covered types Lymphoma 19 trial s 11.0 % of covered types Melanoma 14 trial s 8.1 % of covered types Soft Tissue Sarcoma 13 trial s 7.6 % of covered types * Some trials cover multiple cancer types and are counted once per type. Total counted ( 172 ) may exceed unique trials ( 100 ). Check Your Pet's Eligibility Now Get matched with trials in under 2 minutes Active Clinical Trials Over 100 oncology clinical trials are currently underway across the United States. We have highlighted a selection below to illustrate the collaborative opportunities available to you and your pet today. Trametinib for Canine Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma 📍 New York 🐕 Dog Trametinib for Canine Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma Recruiting Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma Partially Funded A fully funded trial lasting 4 months to treat oral squamous cell carcinoma in dogs using a small molecule inhibitor currently used in human cancer treatment. Start Application 📍 Georgia 🐕 Dog Exploratory IVP Trial for Canine B-cell Lymphoma Recruiting Lymphoma Partially Funded A fully funded trial to test a new oral drug designed to treat canine lymphoma. Start Application 📍