          "text_sha256": "f82d86143618e6cd811612d2cd0909b7f1f37d567b3b71bfc775bc23c1995bf2",
          "text_length": 3855,
          "text_excerpt": "Animal Immune Platform | Platforms | R&D | Vaxcell Bio ANIMAL IMMUNE PLATFORM HOME R&D Platforms Animal Immune Platform VCB-2401 (Vaxleukin-15) Animal-Specific Immuno-Oncology Drugs: Market Insights Korea's First Immuno-Oncology Drug for Dogs Mechanism of Action Manufacturing Product Description Prescription Clinics List GOLDMMUNE VCB-2401 VAXLEUKIN-15 Animal-Specific Immuno-Oncology Drugs: Market Insights Dogs suffer from cancer at rates higher than humans. The incidence of cancer in dogs is significantly elevated compared to humans—lymphoma occurs 2~5 times more often, mammary cancer 4 times, osteosarcoma 8 times, and skin cancer 35 times more frequently in dogs. For dogs aged 8 and older, the cancer incidence rate approaches 40~50%. Despite the growing market for pet medications, the development of new veterinary drugs has not kept pace with demand. Existing pet immuno-oncology drugs are primarily repurposed from human treatments, which often leads to lower efficacy and concerns about side effects when used in animals. In response to this market demand, Vaxcellbio has developed VCB-2401(Vaxleukin-15), an immuno-oncology drug specifically for pets. Pet Cancer Drug Market VCB-2401(Vaxleukin-15): Korea's first immunoadjuvant therapy exclusively for companion dogs VCB-2401 is a recombinant drug developed based on canine interleukin-15, a cytokine secreted by canine white blood cells, using the Escherichia coli expression system. When administered to companion dogs, VCB-2401 activates immune cells such as NK cells and T cells, enhancing their anti-cancer immune functions. This immunotherapy not only shows strong anticancer efficacy but also ensures safety for pets, making it a reliable treatment option for dogs with cancer. In August 2024, the Animal and Plant Quarantine Agency granted product approval for VCB-2401 as the first domestic immuno-oncology drug for companion animals (an adjuvant after mammary tumor surgery). In September 2025, the indications were expanded by granting product approval as an adjuvant treatment for canine lymphoma and mammary tumors. Vaxcellbio plans to expand the indications for VCB-2401 to include feline diseases, following mammary tumors and lymphomas in dogs. VCB-2401(Vaxleukin-15) VCB-2401’s Mechanism of Action When interleukin-15 binds to its receptor, it activates the JAK1 (Janus-associated kinase 1 protein through the beta chain (phosphorylation of tyrosine residues on JAK). This process induces the phosphorylation of STAT3/5 (signal transducer and activator of transcription 3/5) proteins via the gamma chain. During this process, immune cells within the body, such as NK cells and T cells, are activated, thereby enhancing anti-cancer effects. VCB-2401 Manufacturing VCB-2401(Vaxleukin-15) Product Description Name Vaxleukin-15 inj. Category Prescription Drug Indication Anticancer immunotherapy (adjuvant) for dogs affected by mammary tumors and lymphoma Active Ingredient Recombinant Canine IL-15 (Interleukin-15) Information Formulation : Injectable (Recombinant Biologic Drug) Active Ingredient and Dosage : Recombinant canine IL-15 (Canine-derived Interleukin-15) .......... 100 μg Indication/Effectiveness : Immunoadjuvant therapy used in conjunction with surgical (standard therapy) anticancer treatment for dogs with mammary tumors : Immunoadjuvant therapy used in conjunction with chemotherapy (standard therapy) for dogs with lymphoma Dosage and Administration : For Dogs: Dilute 20 μg/kg (0.2 ml per kg body weight) of the drug in 10 ml of sterile saline and administer it slowly (within 10 minutes) via an intravenous catheter. Administer once daily for 4 days, followed by a 10-day rest period, then again administer once daily for another 4 days. Storage : Store in a sealed container. Keep refrigerated between 2-8°C, avoiding freezing, and protect from light.",
